    skos:altLabel 'HFR_GDOP'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Dilution of precision of position {GDOP} by high frequency radar and computation using equations from Chapman et al. (1997)'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The Dilution of Precision (DOP) or Geometric Dilution of Precision (GDOP) is the coefficient of the uncertainty which  relates the uncertainties in radial and velocity vectors. Originally used in satellite navigation but here adapted to the geometry of radial sites. It is a key  index to optimize the configuration and to assess the positioning  precision. First defined in Chapman et al, (1997) On the accuracy of HF radar surface current measurements: Intercomparisons with ship-based  sensors. Journal of Geophysical Research Atmospheres  1021(C8):18737-18748.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P01::HFRGDOP1'^^xsd:string .
