    skos:prefLabel 'Concentration of coloured dissolved organic matter expressed as quinine sulphate equivalent {FDOM QSU} {Gelbstoff} per unit volume of the water body [dissolved plus reactive particulate phase] by in-situ fluorometer'@en ;
    skos:definition 'The quantity of the optically measurable component of coloured (chromophoric) dissolved organic matter (CDOM) that fluoresces when excited with near ultra-violet (UV) light, measured in a unit volume of any body of fresh or salt water by an in-situ fluorometer and calibrated against a quinine sulphate proxy. Often referred to as fluorescent dissolved organic matter (FDOM) when expressed as quinine sulphate equivalent.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P01::QSCDOMX1'^^xsd:string .
