    dc:modified '2024-03-05T14:04:25'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'VolScattering_Beta_p_particles_800nm'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Volume scattering attributable to particles of electromagnetic radiation (800nm wavelength) {Beta(p)} in the water body by in-situ optical backscatter measurement'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Code deprecated on 05/03/2024: created in error. Definition was: The radiant intensity of scattered light from particles in the water body as a function of angle, with the scattering contribution of pure seawater removed, measured at the specified wavelength by an in-situ optical backscattering instrument. Beta(p) is determined by calculating the volume scattering of pure seawater and removing it from the total volume scattering coefficient (Beta) to yield the volume scattering attributable to particles only.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P01::BPVSO800'^^xsd:string .
<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/BVSFO800/2/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/BVSFO800/2/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/P01/current/BVSFO800/>;
    dc:modified '2024-03-05T14:04:23'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel 'VolScattering_Beta_800nm'^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'Volume scattering coefficient of electromagnetic radiation (800nm wavelength) {Beta} in the water body by in-situ optical backscatter measurement'@en ;
    skos:definition 'Code deprecated on 05/03/2024: created in error. Definition was: The radiant intensity of scattered light from the water body as a function of angle, measured at the specified wavelength by an in-situ optical backscattering instrument. Volume scattering coefficient (Beta) is calculated by subtracting dark counts from the raw counts then multiplying by the manufacturer-supplied calibration scale factor.'@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:P01::BVSFO800'^^xsd:string .
